{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrZxVZX76A3bYCe3ziY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013jD86vVzeRG7Uq3CUk1j5A","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050302__x4339a3/work/MashTV-SmashTV-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050302/.cache/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && grep -n \"HOOKS\" my-3d2dge.js | head -20; grep -n \"_sfxBus\" my-3d2dge.js | head; grep -n \"key: 'glyphs'\\|'glyphs'\" my-3d2dge.js | head; grep -n \"class Arcade\\|Arcade = \\|continue(\\|enter(score\" my-3d2dge.js | head -20; cat game/game.js | head -80"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11024,"cache_read_input_tokens":123877,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11024},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"592e1de7-5cd9-4b58-be6b-33507bcad868","uuid":"9e46238c-da09-48fc-9036-35f5b336f05d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:55.146Z","request_id":"req_011CghrZxBxFUPpWAGnDZjsn","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013jD86vVzeRG7Uq3CUk1j5A":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050302__x4339a3/work/MashTV-SmashTV-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050302/.cache/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && grep -n \"HOOKS\" my-3d2dge.js | head -20; grep -n \"_sfxBus\" my-3d2dge.js | head; grep -n \"key: 'glyphs'\\|'glyphs'\" my-3d2dge.js | head; grep -n \"class Arcade\\|Arcade = \\|continue(\\|enter(score\" my-3d2dge.js | head -20; cat game/game.js | head -80"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013jD86vVzeRG7Uq3CUk1j5A","type":"tool_result","content":"316:const HOOKS = { input: [], step: [], enter: [], draw: [], rot: null, frame: null, pose: null, pause: null }, FADES = {};\n475:const _turn = (spr, o) => HOOKS.rot ? HOOKS.rot(spr, o.rot, o.steps) : (warn('rot', 'sprite turns (rot) are left out of this kit (section 2b): the full engine has them'), spr);\n537:HOOKS.rot = rotSprite;\n2219:      this._tg = this._vG; for (const f of HOOKS.draw) f(game, this, this._vG); for (const f of this._overlays) f(this._vG); this._tg = null;\n2232:      for (const f of HOOKS.draw) f(game, this, g);\n2859:    for (const f of HOOKS.enter) f(this, old);\n2877:    for (const f of HOOKS.input) f(this, dt);\n2900:    for (const f of HOOKS.step) f(this, dt);\n2936:    if (this._split && HOOKS.frame) HOOKS.frame(this, shx, shy);   // a split screen: the scene drawn in each viewport (section 10j)\n3303:HOOKS.step.push((g, dt) => {\n3309:HOOKS.enter.push(g => { const J = g._jobs; if (J) for (const j of J.slice()) if (!j.keep) j.cancel(); });\n3509:HOOKS.enter.push((g, old) => { if (old) g.weather = null; });\n3510:HOOKS.step.push((g, dt) => {\n3515:HOOKS.draw.push((g, r, ctx) => { const w = g.weather, S = g._wx; if (w && w.kind && S && WEATHER[w.kind]) _wxDraw(g, r, ctx, S, w, WEATHER[w.kind]); });\n3587:HOOKS.input.push(g => { for (const I of g._players || [g.input]) {   // (each player's own history: game.players)\n3753:HOOKS.input.push((game, dt) => {\n3772:HOOKS.enter.push(game => {   // a scene's start: the others take its keys too (a half each where they share the keyboard); a split ends\n3777:HOOKS.step.push((game, dt) => { if (game._split) for (const v of game._split.vps) _vpCam(game, v, dt); });\n3780:HOOKS.frame = (game, shx, shy) => {\n3910:HOOKS.step.push((game, dt) => { const s = game._saves, sc = game.scene; if (s && sc && (sc.pausable || game.sceneName === 'main')) s.played += dt; });   // time played: the game's scenes, not its titles\n7556:      this._sfxBus = c.createGain(); this._sfxBus.connect(this._master);\n7570:  applyVolume() { if (!this.ctx) return; this._master.gain.value = this.muted ? 0 : this.volume; this._sfxBus.gain.value = this.sfxVolume; this._musBus.gain.value = this.musicVolume * (this._ducked || this.ducked ? .35 : 1); }\n7623:    try { for (const v of Array.isArray(p) ? p : [p]) this._voice(o.vol === undefined ? v : Object.assign({}, v, { vol: (v.vol === undefined ? .3 : v.vol) * o.vol }), this._sfxBus, at, mul); }\n10358:  stage in p.save) or 'over'; then cab.continue(10, done) counts down (done(true): lives back, the score kept).\n10360:  cab.enter(score, mode, done): initials on a letter wheel (up and down turn it, left and right move, confirm takes a\n10389:class Arcade {\n10443:  continue(seconds = 10, done) { this._cont = { t: seconds, done }; this.game.input.consumeAll(); }\n10451:  enter(score, mode = '', done) { this.entry = { score, mode, name: [0, 0, 0], i: 0, done, t: 0 }; this.game.input.consumeAll(); }\n10559:E.Arcade = Arcade;\n// The handoff package's template game: a rooftop thief in the isometric view. Climb onto the roof, take the gem, and\n// don't let the guard in the street watch you for long. It shows what a game is made of (scenes, a TileMap with roofs, a\n// Mover and a Humanoid, input, the camera, a HUD) and the height-aware API: E.Mover climbs any wall (climbAny: jump at\n// it, the stick climbs, jump leaps up, it pulls up at the top) and glides (glide: jump again in the air; a sail drawn\n// over it), both on its stamina, the guard is a plain Body, map.sight and E.inArc for\n// the guard's eyes (they see over the planter, not through the roof), shapes and materials (docs/ASSETS.md: barrels and\n// crates as data, solid with map.solid; the street's cobbles a material), and game.debug for tests and tools. The pause menu,\n// settings, rebinding and full screen come with every game: menu: { controls } names the actions on its Controls screen,\n// and input.label() puts the player's own key or button in a prompt. The night is canvas lighting (game.lights): an\n// ambient, and lights added every draw (a street lamp, the gem's glow), the same in every browser and every check. The\n// HUD is HTML (E.Shell: the objective with its distance, the guard's alert, your keys), over the pixels; the title and\n// end screens are pixel art.\n// Copy it and make it your game. Test it headless: node game/test.mjs. Check it in a browser: node tools/check.mjs game/index.html\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge;\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'snes', expand: true, view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter'],   // expand: full screen at any shape (the HUD anchors to r.W, r.H)\n  menu: { controls: { jump: 'Jump and climb', attack: false, dash: false, skill: false } } });   // (this game uses moves and jump only)\nconst ui = new E.Shell(game);   // the HTML HUD (it keeps the standard pause menu); headless, it draws nothing\nconst ROOF = 32;\nconst map = new E.TileMap({\n  rows: ['############',\n         '#..........#',\n         '#.@........#',\n         '#....p.....#',\n         '#......RRR.#',\n         '#......RGR.#',\n         '#..s...RRR.#',\n         '#..........#',\n         '############'],\n  legend: { '#': 1, R: 2, G: { tile: 2, spawn: 'gem' }, p: 3, '@': 'hero', s: 'guard' },\n  types: { 1: { h: 48, top: '#5a5068', side: '#3e3650', cut: true },\n           2: { h: ROOF, top: '#9a4a3a', side: '#c8b89a', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles' },\n           3: { h: 10, top: '#3e7a3a', side: '#5a4a32', face: 'plank', roof: 'leaves' } },\n  floorMat: 'cobble'   // a material (E.MATERIALS, or '#hex pattern'): the floor, wall faces and tops, shapes' parts all take them\n});\n// set dressing: shapes (E.SHAPES: objects as data, right in every view), solid where they stand (map.solid: walk into one, land on it)\nconst DRESS = [['barrel', 152, 30, { facing: .5 }], ['barrel', 166, 26, { facing: 2 }], ['crate', 22, 120, { facing: .3 }], ['cart', 72, 26, { facing: 0 }]];\nfor (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) map.solid(id, x, y, 0, o);\nconst GEM = E.sprite(['.c.', 'cCc', '.c.'], { c: '#48c8f0', C: '#e8faff' }, 2);\nlet hero, heroRig, guard, guardRig, alert, got, won;\n\nfunction reset() {\n  const h = map.find('hero'), g = map.find('guard');\n  hero = new E.Mover({ x: h.x, y: h.y, r: 5, climbAny: true, climbMax: 24, glide: true, staminaMax: 100 }); hero.facing = 0;   // (the roof, 32 high, is climbed)\n  heroRig = heroRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, hood: true, outfit: 'coat', colors: { cloth: '#3a4a6a', cape: '#2a3a52' } });\n  guard = new E.Body({ x: g.x, y: g.y, r: 5 }); guard.facing = 0; guard.dir = 1;\n  guardRig = guardRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: 'sword', hat: 'helmet', colors: { cloth: '#8a3a32' } });\n  alert = 0; got = false; won = false;\n}\n\nconst title = {\n  update() { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { reset(); game.go('play'); } },\n  draw(r) {\n    r.sky(['#141030', '#3a2a60']);\n    const m = Math.round(r.H / 2);   // centred on any screen\n    r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'ROOFTOP', r.W / 2, m - 52, { scale: 3, align: 'center' }));\n    r.text(('CLIMB WITH ' + game.input.label('jump') + '  TAKE THE GEM  STAY UNSEEN').toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 8, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center' });\n    r.text(('PRESS ' + game.input.label('start')).toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 38, '#ffffff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n  }\n};\n\nconst play = {\n  pausable: true,\n  enter() { game.follow(hero, { z: 16 }); game.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v); game.lights.enabled = true; game.lights.ambient = .5; },\n  exit() { game.lights.enabled = false; ui.hud({}); },\n  update(dt) {\n    const I = game.input, was = !!(hero.wall || hero.action);\n    hero.update(dt, map, I);   // walks, jumps, climbs: the stick and the jump button, through the view\n    if (!was && (hero.wall || hero.action)) game.audio.sfx('jump');\n    // the guard walks the street and watches ahead: its eyes see over the planter, not through the roof\n    guard.vx = guard.dir * 30; guard.update(dt, map);\n    if (guard.x > 112 || guard.hitWall) guard.dir = -1; else if (guard.x < 40) guard.dir = 1;\n    guard.facing = guard.dir > 0 ? 0 : Math.PI;\n    const sees = map.sight(guard, hero) && E.inArc(guard, guard.facing, hero, 110, .6);\n    alert = sees ? alert + dt : Math.max(0, alert - dt * .5);\n    const gem = map.find('gem');\n    if (!got && E.dist(hero, { x: gem.x, y: gem.y, z: ROOF }) < 12) { got = true; game.audio.sfx('coin'); game.flash('#c8f4ff', .15); }\n    if (got && hero.z < 2) { won = true; game.go('end'); }   // back down in the street with it\n    else if (alert > 1.2) { won = false; game.audio.sfx('hurt'); game.go('end'); }\n    // the rigs are posed every step from the bodies' motion; draw only draws them","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"592e1de7-5cd9-4b58-be6b-33507bcad868","uuid":"a05d5a99-17e8-4d1c-8021-e2e0406af07c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:55.179Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"316:const HOOKS = { input: [], step: [], enter: [], draw: [], rot: null, frame: null, pose: null, pause: null }, FADES = {};\n475:const _turn = (spr, o) => HOOKS.rot ? HOOKS.rot(spr, o.rot, o.steps) : (warn('rot', 'sprite turns (rot) are left out of this kit (section 2b): the full engine has them'), spr);\n537:HOOKS.rot = rotSprite;\n2219:      this._tg = this._vG; for (const f of HOOKS.draw) f(game, this, this._vG); for (const f of this._overlays) f(this._vG); this._tg = null;\n2232:      for (const f of HOOKS.draw) f(game, this, g);\n2859:    for (const f of HOOKS.enter) f(this, old);\n2877:    for (const f of HOOKS.input) f(this, dt);\n2900:    for (const f of HOOKS.step) f(this, dt);\n2936:    if (this._split && HOOKS.frame) HOOKS.frame(this, shx, shy);   // a split screen: the scene drawn in each viewport (section 10j)\n3303:HOOKS.step.push((g, dt) =>